content:
The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```java
@Test
public void testSecureConnection() {
    // Code that sets up secure ZooKeeper connection
    connectToZK(KDC_HOST);
}
```
```java
@Test
public void testNonSecureConnection() {
    // Code that sets up non-secure ZooKeeper connection
    connectToZK("localhost");
}
```
Reason:
The tests for secure and non-secure ZooKeeper connections are not properly isolated, causing conflicts when both tests are executed together. The hardcoded retry policy and reliance on the KDC host for authentication can lead to inconsistencies, especially in shared test environments.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
@Test
@Isolation
public void testSecureConnection() {
    // Code that sets up secure ZooKeeper connection
    connectToZK(KDC_HOST);
}
```
```java
@Test
@Isolation
public void testNonSecureConnection() {
    // Code that sets up non-secure ZooKeeper connection
    connectToZK("localhost");
}
```
Reason:
By adding an `@Isolation` annotation (or similar mechanism), the tests for secure and non-secure connections are run in isolation from each other, preventing conflicts. This ensures that the test environments do not interfere, leading to more reliable test outcomes.

